      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm having some trouble with some walnut joinery. i'm cutting dovetails but the tips of the pins keep splintering or tearing out slightly. what am I doing wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Splintering dovetail pins in walnut, a hard wood, is a common frustration, and it often points to a few things. You might be pushing too hard, or perhaps your chisels aren't perfectly sharp, which can cause the wood fibers to tear out instead of cleanly shearing. Try ensuring your chisels are razor-sharp, and approach the cuts with a light, controlled hand, letting the blade do the work. A good setup is key to getting clean cuts, even with stubborn walnut.",
